; Leg EA -- CONTROL for edit 25.  Host SENDS; the Victor receives into A:\.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
;  START THE VICTOR FIRST.  It takes about 40 s to load; wait for the
;  drive to go quiet, then start this.
;
;  Binary under test: D:\CKBB.EXE, md5 c42c3598..., HEAD BEFORE edits 23-26.
;  CONTROL VALUE, SS16bc leg HL: 57.006 s host, elapsed 5950 cs,
;  dec max=450 at #3, 39,564 wire bytes, 1 timeout / 1 resend, 574 cps.
;  A:'s root was 156 entries then and is 184 now, so EA may run SLOWER
;  than HL.  That is exactly why HL's number is not reused (SS16al: the
;  spread is the host, and cross-sitting comparisons are worthless).
;
;  RUN EB IMMEDIATELY AFTER THIS.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPEA.OUT> s16bdEA.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 9600
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bdEA.pkt
send rcvea.dat
statistics
